      "translation": "Schlauer copen, nicht härter"
    },
    {
      "context": "Current UI: OptiScaler/menu/menu_common.cpp",
      "control": "label",
      "english": "Coping is strong with this one...",
      "id": "ingame.menu-common.coping_is_strong_with_this_one_8c12616d",
      "line_breaks": false,
      "placeholders": [],
      "preserve": [],
      "revision": 1,
      "section": "menu-common",
      "surface": "in_game",
      "translation": "Das Coping ist stark in diesem..."
    },
    {
      "context": "Current UI: OptiScaler/menu/menu_common.cpp",
      "control": "label",
      "english": "Corresponds to amount of accumulation added per frame",
      "id": "ingame.menu-common.corresponds_to_amount_of_accumulation_added_per__48f6baf5",
      "line_breaks": false,
      "placeholders": [],
      "preserve": [],
      "revision": 1,
      "section": "menu-common",
      "surface": "in_game",
      "translation": "Entspricht der Menge an Akkumulation, die pro Frame hinzugefügt wird"
    },
    {
      "context": "Current UI: OptiScaler/menu/menu_common.cpp",
      "control": "paragraph",
      "english": "Corresponds to amount of accumulation added per frame\nat pixel coordinate where disocclusion occured or when\nreactive mask value is > 0.0f. Decreasing this and \ndrawing the ghosting object (IE no mv) to reactive mask \nwith value close to 1.0f can decrease temporal ghosting.\nDecreasing this could result in more thin feature pixels flickering.",
      "id": "ingame.menu-common.corresponds_to_amount_of_accumulation_added_per__a71e0ab2",
      "line_breaks": true,
      "placeholders": [],
      "preserve": [],
      "revision": 1,
      "section": "menu-common",
      "surface": "in_game",
      "translation": "Entspricht der Menge an Akkumulation, die pro Frame an der Pixelkoordinate hinzugefügt wird,\nan der Disokklusion aufgetreten ist oder wenn der Wert der reaktiven Maske > 0.0f ist.\nEine Verringerung und das Zeichnen des Ghosting-Objekts (d. h. kein MV) auf die\nreaktive Maske mit einem Wert nahe 1.0f kann das temporale Ghosting verringern.\nEine Verringerung kann dazu führen, dass feine Pixel-Details stärker flackern."
    },
